# Week 1: Digital Literacy, Computer Fundamentals, and Professional Development
ALGURAWY CYBERHUB ACADEMY  
Sponsored by DR. BUKAR USMAN FOUNDATION  

## 🎯 Learning Outcomes
By the end of Week One, participants should be able to:
- Identify major computer hardware components and explain their functions.
- Differentiate between system software and application software.
- Organize files and folders using appropriate naming conventions.
- Install and uninstall software responsibly.
- Use Microsoft Office and Google Workspace for productivity and collaboration.
- Apply Internet and digital communication skills.
- Compose professional emails.
- Demonstrate responsible, ethical, and safe use of digital technologies.
- Exhibit appropriate workplace behaviour and professional conduct.

---

## 📘 Core Topics
- Programme orientation & SIWES expectations  
- Digital economy careers (cybersecurity, software development, networking, cloud computing, data analysis, forensics, web development, marketing)  
- Professional ethics (integrity, confidentiality, accountability, respect, competence, responsible technology use)  
- Computer hardware assembly & maintenance  
- Operating systems (Windows vs Linux)  
- File & data management  
- System vs application software  
- Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)  
- Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Slides, Drive)  
- Internet fundamentals & professional email writing  

---

## 🧪 Practical Exercises
1. Assemble and disassemble a desktop computer safely.  
2. Install Windows or Ubuntu in a controlled lab environment.  
3. Create a SIWES folder structure with subfolders for each week.  
4. Prepare a two‑page SIWES Training Report in Microsoft Word.  
5. Create a student attendance spreadsheet in Excel.  
6. Prepare a short presentation titled **“My Technology Career Goal”** in PowerPoint.  
7. Use Google Docs to collaboratively edit a document with a classmate.  
8. Write a professional email to your SIWES supervisor requesting permission to join a training activity.  

